Size: the content shell without its web-test runner.

The content shell links the harness Chromium's web tests run in
(//content/web_test, with gmock and the test controllers): about a MiB of
the engine that only --run-web-tests reaches. A GN argument,
content_shell_web_tests, leaves it out; ShellMainDelegate's web-test paths
are compiled only with it, under CONTENT_SHELL_WEB_TESTS, which
content_shell_app exports so that every user of its header sees the same
class.

Off in profiles/slim.gn. Upstream's default is unchanged.

--- a/content/shell/BUILD.gn
+++ b/content/shell/BUILD.gn
@@ -58,8 +58,19 @@
   }
 }
 
-# Web test support not built on android, but is everywhere else.
-support_web_tests = !is_android
+declare_args() {
+  # Web test support not built on android, but is everywhere else. zebkit's
+  # slim profile leaves it out: the shell is the engine there, and no web
+  # tests run in it.
+  content_shell_web_tests = !is_android
+}
+support_web_tests = content_shell_web_tests
+
+config("web_tests_config") {
+  if (support_web_tests) {
+    defines = [ "CONTENT_SHELL_WEB_TESTS" ]
+  }
+}
 
